sn36.4:3.1 starts: A weakling of little strength
sn36.4:3.2 starts: Who weeps out loud and wails:
sn36.4:3.3 starts: He has not risen up in the bottomless
sn36.4:3.4 starts: Nor has he even gained a foothold.
sn36.5:2.1 starts: One who has seen the pleasant as painful
sn36.5:2.2 starts: And the painful as a dart,
sn36.5:2.3 starts: Seen as impermanent the peaceful feeling
sn36.5:2.4 starts: Neither painful nor pleasant:
sn4.11:3.1 starts: “Even if you make this Vulture Peak
sn4.11:3.2 starts: Quake all over in its entirety,
sn4.11:3.3 starts: The enlightened are not perturbed,
sn4.11:3.4 starts: For they are are fully liberated.”
sn4.16:5.1 starts: “Though they seek him everywhere,
sn4.16:5.2 starts: Mara and his army do not find him:
sn4.16:5.3 starts: The one thus detached, secure,
sn4.16:5.4 starts: Who has gone beyond all ’fetters.”
sn4.17:4.1 starts: “But when he has transcended this,
sn4.17:4.2 starts: The mindful disciple of the Buddha
sn4.17:4.3 starts: Shines radiantly like the sun,
sn4.17:4.4 starts: Having surmounted Mara’s realm.”
sn4.1:6.1 starts: By developing the path to enlightenment—
sn4.1:6.2 starts: Virtue, concentration, and wisdom—
sn4.1:6.3 starts: I have attained supreme purity:
sn4.1:6.4 starts: You’re defeated, End-maker!”
sn4.20:4.1 starts: “How could a person incline to sensual pleasures
sn4.20:4.2 starts: Who has seen the source whence suffering springs?
sn4.20:4.3 starts: Having known acquisition as a tie in the
sn4.20:4.4 starts: A person should train for its removal.”
sn4.21:4.1 starts: “How could a person incline to sensual pleasures
sn4.21:4.2 starts: Who has seen the source whence suffering springs?
sn4.21:4.3 starts: Having known acquisition as a tie in the
sn4.21:4.4 starts: A person should train for its removal.”
sn4.23:3.1 starts: “O great hero, great in wisdom,
sn4.23:3.2 starts: Blazing forth with power and glory!
sn4.23:3.3 starts: I worship your feet, One with Vision,
sn4.23:3.4 starts: Who has overcome all enmity and fear.
